From bd2946da642cadbb88c0623ea7cb2f02b88ab3f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ville=20Kivel=C3=A4?= <vkivela@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:55:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] extensions: report where a window is, as the application says

chrome.windows answered with one window carrying an id, focus, incognito,
type, state and tabs, and no left, top, width or height. Chrome always
reports all four. Bitwarden places its passkey prompt at
window.left + window.width - popupWidth - 15, which without them is NaN,
and the schema refuses the windows.create that follows:

  Error at property 'left': Invalid type: expected integer, found number.

Where a window is on screen is only the application's to know, so the
engine asks it. QWebEngineExtensionManager::setWindowGeometryProvider
takes a function that is called with the page the call came from, a
QWebEnginePage or a WebEngineView, or with null for a call no page is
behind, such as a worker's. Every window the engine reports carries the
four numbers, windows.create's and populated ones included.

Without a provider, or with an invalid answer, the window is at 0, 0 and
as large as the asking view, or the active tab's view for a worker, so an
extension always gets four integers.

The engine calls a copy of the provider, so a provider that replaces
itself while it is called is not destroyed under its own call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
